tasks.prompt:
A parking garage stores each session as a JSON document with a "zone" (Text), "level" (Int), "duration_minutes" (Int), and "paid" (Bool). The following 4 sessions are given:

session1 = {"zone": "A", "level": 2, "duration_minutes": 95, "paid": true}
session2 = {"zone": "B", "level": 1, "duration_minutes": 140, "paid": false}
session3 = {"zone": "A", "level": 3, "duration_minutes": 60, "paid": true}
session4 = {"zone": "C", "level": 2, "duration_minutes": 180, "paid": false}

Write a program that prints a summary report. Output format, exactly one line per session, in order:

ZONE <zone> | LEVEL <level> | MIN <duration_minutes> | <PAID or UNPAID>

After the session lines, print one final line:

PAID <count> / <total>

where <count> is the number of sessions with paid=true and <total> is the number of sessions.

Example for a single session with zone A, level 2, duration 95, paid true:
ZONE A | LEVEL 2 | MIN 95 | PAID

No trailing spaces on any line.
